
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
S6 · Progress, logging and cancellation (ctx.mcpReq)
SDK: ctx.mcpReq.notify (progress), ctx.mcpReq.log, ctx.mcpReq.signal, client.callTool({ onprogress, signal }), client.setLoggingLevel
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

── Progress — rank_students reports every 10 students ────────────────────────

▶ With onprogress → server sends notifications/progress
  callTool({"name":"rank_students","arguments":{"scope":"all","top":3},"options":{"onprogress":"fn"}})
  ✔ 9ms → 
    {
      "progressUpdates": [
        {
          "progress": 10,
          "total": 40,
          "message": "Scored 10/40 students"
        },
        {
          "progress": 20,
          "total": 40,
          "message": "Scored 20/40 students"
        },
        {
          "progress": 30,
          "total": 40,
          "message": "Scored 30/40 students"
        },
        {
          "progress": 40,
          "total": 40,
          "message": "Scored 40/40 students"
        }
      ],
      "top3": [
        "Võ Hoàng Bình 4",
        "Hoàng Thu Trang 4",
        "Phạm Thị Lan 4"
      ]
    }

▶ Without onprogress → no progressToken, no notifications
  callTool({"name":"rank_students","arguments":{"scope":"all","top":3}})
  ✔ 3ms → 
    {
      "newProgressUpdates": 0
    }

── Logging — client.setLoggingLevel filters ctx.mcpReq.log (2025-era session) 
   ℹ MCP logging is deprecated in protocol 2026-07-28 (SEP-2577); on 2026 connections the level is sent per request.

▶ setLoggingLevel("debug") then callTool
  setLoggingLevel + callTool({"level":"debug","name":"query_table","arguments":{"table":"students","filters":[{"column":"class_id","operator":"eq","value":"IT01"}],"limit":1}})
  ✔ 2ms → 
    {
      "logMessagesReceived": [
        "info: \"query_table students: 11 of 41 rows match\""
      ]
    }

▶ setLoggingLevel("info") then callTool
  setLoggingLevel + callTool({"level":"info","name":"query_table","arguments":{"table":"students","filters":[{"column":"class_id","operator":"eq","value":"IT01"}],"limit":1}})
  ✔ 0ms → 
    {
      "logMessagesReceived": [
        "info: \"query_table students: 11 of 41 rows match\""
      ]
    }

▶ setLoggingLevel("error") then callTool
  setLoggingLevel + callTool({"level":"error","name":"query_table","arguments":{"table":"students","filters":[{"column":"class_id","operator":"eq","value":"IT01"}],"limit":1}})
  ✔ 0ms → 
    {
      "logMessagesReceived": []
    }

── Cancellation — the client aborts; the handler sees ctx.mcpReq.signal ──────

▶ legacy era: abort after 350 ms
  callTool({"name":"recalculate_all_gpas","arguments":{"students":20},"options":{"signal":"AbortSignal"}})
  ✖ 352ms → SdkError (code REQUEST_TIMEOUT): user pressed Stop
   ℹ server side: stopped after 4/20: user pressed Stop

▶ modern era: abort after 350 ms
  callTool({"name":"recalculate_all_gpas","arguments":{"students":20},"options":{"signal":"AbortSignal"}})
  ✖ 352ms → SdkError (code REQUEST_TIMEOUT): user pressed Stop
   ℹ server side: stopped after 4/20: SdkError: Connection closed

✔ 7 steps (2 expected/unexpected errors) — saved outputs/examples/s6-logging-progress-cancel.json
